        </g>
      </svg>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="h-feat">A growing list of features for a whole variety of proven use-cases</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="features">
        <article class="fgroup">
          <h3>Data and storage</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt>Database</dt><dd>GORM on pure-Go SQLite, with split writer and reader pools.</dd>
            <dt>Migrations</dt><dd>Additive migrations, applied at startup in a safe order.</dd>
            <dt>Mergeable store</dt><dd>Append-only event streams with a deterministic merge.</dd>
            <dt>Blobs</dt><dd>Content-addressed files on object storage, with presigned URLs.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article class="fgroup">
          <h3>Sign-in and security</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt>Sessions</dt><dd>Revocable server-side sessions, with step-up re-auth for sensitive routes.</dd>
            <dt>CSRF</dt><dd>An origin check on every mutating request. No tokens to forget.</dd>
            <dt>Owner scoping</dt><dd>Someone else's row answers 404, proven by a two-user test suite.</dd>
            <dt>Magic links</dt><dd>Email sign-in that upgrades to Keymail where it can.</dd>
            <dt>Passwords</dt><dd>Email and password, rate-limited per account.</dd>
            <dt>Passkeys</dt><dd>WebAuthn as a second factor, with recovery codes.</dd>
            <dt>Encryption</dt><dd>P-256 sealing and signing, with a matching browser module.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article class="fgroup">
          <h3>Screens and content</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt>Design system</dt><dd>27 components and design tokens, light and dark.</dd>
            <dt>Manifests</dt><dd>Declare a resource and get its store, actions and screens.</dd>
            <dt>Localization</dt><dd>Locale-aware routes, translations with fallback, and a catalog check before you ship.</dd>
            <dt>Scaffolding</dt><dd><code>rastrillo new</code> gives you a working app with passing tests.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article class="fgroup">
          <h3>Background work</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt>Jobs</dt><dd>Background tasks with a status page that works without JavaScript.</dd>
            <dt>Live updates</dt><dd>Server-Sent Events where supported, plain polling where not.</dd>
            <dt>Scheduling</dt><dd>Timers and recurring jobs that survive restarts and sleeping apps.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article class="fgroup">
          <h3>Agents and platform</h3>
          <dl>
            <dt>SKILL.md</dt><dd>The whole framework in one file an agent can load.</dd>
            <dt>Agent tools</dt><dd>Actions opt in as tools, with consent and attribution.</dd>
            <dt>Hibernation</dt><dd>Apps sleep when idle and wake on the next request.</dd>
            <dt>One binary</dt><dd><code>go build</code> produces the whole app. No bundler, no runtime.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>

